Research interests: • To develop new technologies for renewable energy and environmental protection
Email: ycleung@hku.hk Website: https://www.mech.hku.hk/academic-staff/Leung-DYC
The Al-CO2 battery project strives to create an affordable, highly efficient, and eco-friendly energy storage solution by harnessing CO2 as the fuel at the cathode and employing aluminium as the anode material. The research is concentrated on enhancing catalysts, fine-tuning battery design, and seamlessly integrating it with renewable energy systems. Al-CO2 batteries have the potential to enhance energy storage by capturing and utilizing CO2, thereby making a substantial contribution to global initiatives aimed at combating climate change and minimizing greenhouse gas emissions.
Novelty
Utilizes CO2 as fuel for reversible battery;
Employs non-noble, cost-effective catalysts, such as nitrogen-doped carbon nanotubes, for CO2 electroreduction;
Optimizes battery design and operation, enhancing performance and efficiency in various conditions;
Seamlessly integrates with renewable energy systems for combined energy storage and CO2 capture applications.
(a) Schematic diagram of an Al-CO2 battery; (b) Prototype of the Al-CO2 battery; (c) TEM image of the N-CNT cathode.
(a) Battery performance in pure CO2 and in CO2 / O2 mixture (99:1) (b) Enlarged charge-discharge curve; (c) Performance of the Al-CO2 /O2 battery under different current densities, and (d) Cycle stability test of the Al-CO2 /O2 battery.

Eligibility: Students studying an MSc degree program administered by the Faculty of Engineering in the Academic Year 2023-2024
Tam Wing Fan Innovation Wing (Inno Wing) provides an open environment to foster interdisciplinary innovations among undergraduate students and teachers in Engineering and Technology. This collaborative space contains state-of-the-art facilities which enables curriculum innovations focusing on hands-on and experiential learning activities. Inno Wing is a platform to encourage the young generation to explore the world, to create opportunities for them to learn about the needs of the underprivileged, and to acquire practical hands-on experience in developing solutions with real-world impact.
The Innovation Tutorship Training Scheme (ITTS) aims to encourage fresh graduates of HKU’s Engineering undergraduate programs to further equip themselves by pursuing an MSc degree program administered by the Faculty of Engineering, while also participating in tutorship training at Inno Wing. This comprehensive program provides an invaluable learning opportunity for tutors, which emphasizes the practical application of innovative engineering skills into the real world
Hands-on skills on operating makerspace equipment in Inno Wing, such as 3D printing equipment, acrylic laser cutting and engraving machine and etc;
Knowledge of CAD-related software such as Ultimaker Cura, Prusa slicer, SOLIDWORKS, and CorelDRAW; and
Skills on conducting training workshops individually
The appointee will perform the following assigned duties in Inno Wing for one year under a roster.
Assist student members in the usage of makerspace facilities;
Lead visiting tours showcasing Inno Wing’s unique facilities and student projects to visitors from various backgrounds;
Conduct workshops on makerspace equipment such as (1) 3D printers and (2) laser cutting and engraving machines;
Share experience with the next tutor cohort before the end of the scheme; and
Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Inno Wing

